  "articleBody": "Considering a lever faucet? They're super popular for a reason! One of the main things people ask about is how they connect, especially the hot and cold lines, and whether they need a deck plate. Generally, lever faucets are designed to be quite user-friendly in terms of installation. You'll want to make sure your new faucet's style and design will fit your sink's hole configuration. If your current sink has multiple holes for separate hot/cold handles, you might need a deck plate to cover them if you're switching to a single-lever design. Also, think about the handle itself – is it comfortable and easy to use for everyone in your household? That's a key buying criterion. The type of supply-line fittings required is another important check, so make sure they match your existing plumbing or plan for adapters. If you find your shutoff valves are old, leaky, or just plain faulty when you go to install a new lever faucet, or if you realize the sink cutout needs to be modified for a perfect fit, that's definitely a situation where calling a qualified pro like HH Remodeling LLC can save you a lot of hassle. We serve Denver and all the surrounding communities and can ensure a smooth, leak-free installation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
